{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-06T08:54:18.222Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Implementation**\n- `src/core/foundation/config-gates.ts`: added `commitRetries` (default 2, optional in the interface) validated by the existing `nonNegativeInteger` helper.\n- `src/core/run/dead-commit.ts`: `commitDeadTask` now removes any existing `.run/dead/<n>.patch` before calling `patch()`, so a stale patch never grows into the new one.\n- `src/watcher/commit-catch-up.ts` (new): `catchUpWorktreeCommits` implements all four steps — non-`commit_failed` halts left alone, budget counted from `change.jsonl` since the last human retry, pending dead records committed in order, and a `commit_failed` halt cleared via `retrySpec(..., { automatic: true })` with the catch-up log line.\n- `src/watcher/loop.ts`: invokes the catch-up right after the reaper and before `runAutomaticRetries`, skipping the change when it returns false.\n- `tests/commit-catch-up.test.ts` (new): covers every catch-up scenario, the stale-patch case via `commitDeadTask`, and the gate key's default/invalid cases via `loadConfig`/`defineConfig`, using a real worktree and `pre-commit` hook.\n\n**Verification**\n- Task verify: 38 tests pass.\n- `pnpm verify`: passes (3341 CLI tests, 114 UI tests, both typechecks, build, lint).\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/152-halt-self-recovery/.run/results/1.md`."}}
